-- ── hand-written: who may read and write the two logs ───────────────────────────────────────────
-- Recovery is worked by the recovery officer, the owner, the accountant and the sales manager;
-- the auditor reads it (the founder's decision, 2026-11-14). Customers belong to the whole
-- company, so these rows do too. A row is written as the member writing it, at the moment of
-- writing: the database's own clock, and Pakistan's date for the day a promise was made, so a
-- promise cannot be dated back to take in money that came before it. The date is read from the
-- statement's own clock, not the transaction's, so a transaction held open past midnight cannot
-- date a promise to the day before. Nothing is updated or deleted by the app.
REVOKE ALL ON public.customer_follow_ups, public.payment_promises FROM anon, authenticated, service_role;
